  "notes": "A formal, legal term for abandonment. Also functions as a suru verb ({遺棄|いき}する). Most commonly encountered in news and legal contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {死体|したい}{遺棄|いき} — abandonment of a body (a criminal charge)\n- {遺棄|いき}{罪|ざい} — crime of abandonment\n- {遺棄|いき}する — to abandon, to desert\n- {化学兵器|かがくへいき}の{遺棄|いき} — abandonment of chemical weapons\n- {保護|ほご}{責任者|せきにんしゃ}{遺棄|いき} — abandonment by a person with duty of care\n\nLEGAL CONTEXT:\n{遺棄|いき}{罪|ざい} is a crime under Japanese law that includes abandoning a person who needs care, or abandoning a dead body. {死体|したい}{遺棄|いき} (abandonment of a corpse) is one of the most commonly reported charges in crime news.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {放棄|ほうき} — abandonment, renunciation (broader, includes rights and claims)\n- {投棄|とうき} — dumping, disposal (of waste or objects)\n- {廃棄|はいき} — disposal, scrapping (of documents, equipment)",
